# Gestion Annonces API And Validation

- Use the module structure from the spec: `controller`, `service`, `repository`, `entity`, `dto`, `mapper`, `websocket`.
- Listings API: `POST /api/listings`, `GET /api/listings`, `GET /api/listings/{id}`, `GET /api/listings/search`.
- Comments API: `POST /api/listings/{id}/comments`, `GET /api/listings/{id}/comments`.
- Group API: `POST /api/groups/{id}/join`, `GET /api/groups/{id}`, `DELETE /api/groups/{id}/leave`, `GET /api/groups/{id}/participants`.
- Favorites API: `POST /api/listings/{id}/favorite`, `DELETE /api/listings/{id}/favorite`.
- Validate on the backend even if the frontend already validates.
- Mandatory backend checks: required fields, entity existence, permissions, current listing/group state, parent-child comment consistency, attachment validity, quantity limits, uniqueness rules, and abuse/moderation rules.
- Validate files: accepted extensions, MIME type when possible, max size, max count, reject empty files, and store safely.
- Validate comment rules: non-empty content, max length, anti-spam, moderation path, listing existence.
- Validate group join rules at the last possible moment to avoid stale quantity/state decisions.
- Keep implementation aligned with the main scenarios from the spec: create listing, explore/search, comment, join/leave group, favorite, realtime updates.
